WEBVTT

01:39.240 --> 01:42.990
<b>Today at 21:00</b>

01:49.000 --> 01:51.500
Coronation of Her Majesty Dorothea

01:49.000 --> 01:51.500
<b>New Imperial Coronation</b>

01:49.000 --> 01:51.500
<b>Starting Soon</b>

01:51.500 --> 01:54.000
<b>New Imperial Coronation</b>

01:51.500 --> 01:54.000
<b>Starting Soon</b>

01:57.260 --> 02:00.800
The coronation will begin shortly.

02:01.910 --> 02:03.860
Looks, it's Little Redia.

02:04.080 --> 02:05.770
He's so cute.

02:08.610 --> 02:12.270
Oz here. No problems on the Central Avenue.

02:17.980 --> 02:19.790
It's a peaceful night.

02:29.650 --> 02:35.080
<i>The 23rd emperor of the Redia Empire,</i>

02:35.080 --> 02:41.280
<i>His Majesty, Emperor Goethe, 
brought about the Gear Expansion.</i>

02:41.800 --> 02:46.190
<i>Through it, human civilization 
made rapid progress,</i>

02:46.190 --> 02:51.560
<i>and we gained the strength to carve out 
a new future for ourselves.</i>

02:51.560 --> 02:55.550
<i>We no longer need the power of the witches.</i>

02:55.550 --> 03:00.320
<i>Our scientific and military might 
seized dignity for humankind.</i>

03:00.820 --> 03:05.030
<i>And the kind Emperor Goethe always extended</i>

03:05.030 --> 03:10.100
<i>a hand to us as he walked 
with us side by side.</i>

03:11.320 --> 03:12.570
<i>However...</i>

03:14.160 --> 03:20.220
<i>Not even our beloved emperor 
could overcome his illness.</i>

03:21.640 --> 03:27.720
<i>He brought prosperity to 
our nation—nay, the world,</i>

03:27.720 --> 03:32.630
<i>and the people of Redia have endured 
sleepless nights without our emperor.</i>

03:33.560 --> 03:37.390
<i>But that ended with last night.</i>

03:39.240 --> 03:43.760
<i>Our nation welcomes its new monarch.</i>

03:44.120 --> 03:46.240
Ten, nine,

03:46.240 --> 03:49.240
eight, seven, six,

03:49.240 --> 03:52.750
five, four, three, two,

03:53.010 --> 03:54.610
one!

04:05.040 --> 04:08.480
Please welcome Her Majesty, Queen Dorothea!

04:34.000 --> 04:36.500
Coronation of Her Majesty, Dorothea

04:39.000 --> 04:39.340
Standing ovation!

04:39.000 --> 04:39.960
Incredible outfits. Thank you!

04:39.170 --> 04:40.590
I'd still follow her even if she raised taxes! 
In fact, I'd love to pay more!

04:39.750 --> 04:41.210
The new queen is super young! Totally my type

04:40.380 --> 04:41.590
I see only hope in this country's future

04:40.960 --> 04:41.590
What a historic moment! I'm euphoric 
that I'm getting to see it in real time

04:57.730 --> 04:57.900
No one can replace her! Too cute!

04:57.730 --> 04:58.440
Has a fan club been established yet?!! I'd totally join lol

04:58.270 --> 04:58.650
Long live the queen \(^o^)/ Long live the queen \(^o^)/

04:58.480 --> 04:59.480
Y-Your Majesty! Oh... oh... (speechless)

04:58.650 --> 04:59.650
I haven't been this excited in a while. 
Beauty heals the heart.

04:59.480 --> 04:59.820
Little sister of the people, 
wife of the people, fave 
of the people lol As the 
queen, she can be all of them!

04:59.690 --> 05:00.110
I looove the queen, too!

04:59.860 --> 05:00.440
Whoaaa she's so pretty

05:11.950 --> 05:12.200
She must be a goddess

05:11.950 --> 05:12.490
Is she a fairy?

05:11.950 --> 05:12.910
Is she a goddess?

05:11.990 --> 05:13.330
The supreme goddess!

05:12.410 --> 05:13.450
So pretty!

05:12.410 --> 05:13.450
So cute!

05:13.040 --> 05:13.790
I want to become a road so she'll step on me

05:13.040 --> 05:14.080
I'd gladly lick her shoes. Her legs, too.

05:13.040 --> 05:14.460
Stop turning "queen"
 into a brand new fetish lol

05:13.580 --> 05:14.710
I'm not getting monarch vibes from her.
 She must be a goddess or something.

05:14.040 --> 05:14.710
How was someone this beautiful born? 
She's on another level...

05:17.960 --> 05:22.760
<i>Hello, everyone! I love all of you!</i>

05:56.390 --> 05:58.980
A witch and the monarch of humanity?

05:58.980 --> 06:00.760
What has the world come to?

06:01.720 --> 06:08.040
She exterminated her own kind with 
science while ruling the world as its queen.

06:28.920 --> 06:31.720
This witch known as Dorothea...

06:33.120 --> 06:35.870
is even crazier than predicted.

07:26.920 --> 07:30.880
Meanwhile, in the Wastelands of the Southern Hemisphere

07:30.420 --> 07:35.430
Huh. Her Majesty Dorothea is divine.

07:35.880 --> 07:39.890
But this kinda feels like...

07:40.730 --> 07:43.900
Head of the Redia Empire 
National Intelligence Agency 
\h\h\h\hSenior Director Shirousagi

07:42.430 --> 07:48.400
my childhood friend 
has become the school's idol.

07:50.980 --> 07:54.320
I know. The mission comes first, right?

07:57.410 --> 08:00.160
He's a smart kid.

08:00.720 --> 08:05.630
He broke the device he took 
from Yamato, so I can't use it to trace him.

08:07.440 --> 08:09.170
Fine, then.

08:09.610 --> 08:12.110
I'll have to find him the hard way.

08:15.850 --> 08:18.970
The boy loved by a goddess.

08:31.190 --> 08:33.940
So, what are you going to do?

08:35.070 --> 08:39.820
Just so you know, I'm not 
going to stop seeking revenge.

08:41.080 --> 08:45.230
I actually have a suggestion.

08:45.230 --> 08:50.660
There are kind people like 
Mr. Punch and his friends, so...

08:53.080 --> 08:57.240
So I should avoid 
fighting people like them?

08:57.610 --> 08:58.850
I don't think so.

09:02.200 --> 09:06.600
I've allowed you to accompany me, 
but let me make one thing clear.

09:07.180 --> 09:09.650
Don't get in my way.

09:13.280 --> 09:14.480
Okay.

09:20.600 --> 09:24.200
Also... Also!

09:24.200 --> 09:26.120
Uh, y-yes?

09:26.570 --> 09:29.880
I want to confirm your 
"Love Magic" makes men fall

09:29.880 --> 09:33.730
in love with you so you can control them.

09:33.730 --> 09:35.040
Is that correct?

09:36.130 --> 09:37.100
Yes.

09:37.630 --> 09:42.810
Then why didn't you cast that magic on me?

09:44.800 --> 09:47.030
That day, in Redia,

09:48.700 --> 09:51.280
when we first met.

09:52.330 --> 09:58.040
Ophelia must've ordered you to kidnap me, 
even if it meant using that magic.

09:58.040 --> 10:00.870
After all, that would've 
been the most effective way.

10:02.800 --> 10:06.120
But you didn't cast any spells on me.

10:06.820 --> 10:08.010
Why not?

10:08.450 --> 10:10.620
Why did you try to convince me instead?

10:12.710 --> 10:19.280
Because you wouldn't have liked our 
first meeting to go like that, would you?

10:34.320 --> 10:37.140
<i>Yeah, that would've sucked.</i>

11:16.210 --> 11:18.230
Sand Land...

11:18.560 --> 11:22.480
It's a small town, but it's in ruins.

11:24.350 --> 11:27.560
Maybe there's no one here.

11:34.270 --> 11:36.400
Wait here.

11:36.400 --> 11:39.620
I'm going to look around. Got it?

11:39.620 --> 11:41.770
What? Hey, wait.

11:42.020 --> 11:43.760
I'll go with you.

11:44.890 --> 11:47.890
I won't get in your way. Please.

11:49.610 --> 11:52.960
Anyway, what's with the bag?

11:53.920 --> 11:55.140
Oh, this?

11:55.140 --> 11:58.640
Mr. Punch gave me a bunch 
of things to take with me.

11:58.640 --> 12:04.620
I've got canned goods, dried bread, 
bandages, blankets, and drinks.

12:04.620 --> 12:06.920
Drinks? You mean alcohol?

12:06.920 --> 12:09.980
Also, look! This thing is amazing!

12:10.350 --> 12:13.410
Just watch. Let me turn it on.

12:17.910 --> 12:21.400
Tada! It's a snowman tent.

12:21.400 --> 12:22.770
Mr. Punch said...

12:22.770 --> 12:25.940
It's a little cramped 
for a young couple though!

12:25.940 --> 12:27.180
When he gave it to me.

12:27.180 --> 12:31.940
But I tried it out, and it's actually 
surprisingly large and warm inside.

12:32.150 --> 12:34.050
Uh-huh. Well, I'm going now.

12:34.050 --> 12:36.690
Wait, what?!

12:44.860 --> 12:47.440
It really is a ghost town.

12:48.530 --> 12:51.770
I wonder if there are actually ghosts here.

12:58.320 --> 13:00.650
<i>No signs of fighting.</i>

13:01.100 --> 13:02.960
<i>So why isn't anyone here?</i>

13:13.400 --> 13:16.730
This seems to be 
the biggest building in town.

13:17.300 --> 13:19.840
Hopefully, we can find some information here.

13:20.730 --> 13:22.500
Is it some kind of store?

13:23.250 --> 13:24.750
I'm not sure.

13:31.990 --> 13:35.600
It's pretty run down. Watch your step.

13:35.600 --> 13:37.000
Yeah, I kno—

13:45.880 --> 13:48.350
S-Sorry.

13:52.530 --> 13:55.280
Wait! I can't see where I'm going!

13:56.760 --> 14:02.490
Ow! The floor bit me!

13:56.770 --> 14:00.400
<i>SKREEE</i>

14:04.150 --> 14:10.030
<i>RUMBLE</i>

14:05.950 --> 14:08.250
I'm so sorry...

14:12.390 --> 14:14.760
I told you to be careful.

14:14.760 --> 14:17.280
If you're too noisy, I'll leave you behind.

14:20.900 --> 14:23.940
<i>Do you need help, miss?</i>

14:25.800 --> 14:29.040
<i>Do you need help, miss?</i>

14:34.050 --> 14:37.060
A gh-gh-ghost?

14:37.060 --> 14:40.510
Adonis, it's a ghost! An actual ghost!

14:41.060 --> 14:43.700
<i>Welcome to the Sand Land police station.</i>

14:43.700 --> 14:46.800
<i>The current time is 13:22.</i>

14:46.800 --> 14:49.500
<i>For lost articles, turn right 
at the end of the hallway.</i>

14:49.500 --> 14:51.570
<i>For traffic, head straight ahead.</i>

14:51.570 --> 14:55.840
<i>For residential problems, head left.</i>

14:55.840 --> 14:58.240
<i>Do you have your citizen card?</i>

14:58.240 --> 15:00.400
Huh? What?

15:00.400 --> 15:02.440
It's a hologram.

15:03.290 --> 15:05.840
Mr. Hologram?

15:06.170 --> 15:08.720
You know him?

15:08.720 --> 15:11.240
It's just a three-dimensional image.

15:11.240 --> 15:14.100
This is ridiculous. Let's keep going.

15:14.100 --> 15:15.410
Okay.

15:15.410 --> 15:16.890
I see.

15:16.890 --> 15:20.100
The people who worked here were 
police officers who protected everyone.

15:20.560 --> 15:24.850
Yeah, not that there's anyone 
to protect anymore.

15:25.230 --> 15:30.440
Well, we mean no harm. Excuse us.

15:30.440 --> 15:31.830
I'm leaving you behind.

15:31.830 --> 15:33.790
Hey, wait.

15:34.330 --> 15:36.950
<i>Welcome to the Sand Land police station.</i>

15:36.950 --> 15:40.120
<i>The current time is 13:23.</i>

16:12.130 --> 16:13.600
Jail cells.

16:13.600 --> 16:16.290
Neither of us have pleasant 
memories associated with these.

16:25.650 --> 16:28.670
<i>Oh, my beloved Sasha.</i>

16:29.470 --> 16:30.950
Ow...

16:30.950 --> 16:32.310
Sorry, Adonis.

16:32.310 --> 16:34.720
Hush. I hear something.

16:37.730 --> 16:42.370
<i>Your eyes are clear and beautiful.</i>

16:41.240 --> 16:42.370
A song?

16:43.570 --> 16:53.680
<i>Even if the light in them goes out,</i>

16:55.260 --> 17:06.380
<i>we'll still have good morning kisses, 
humming in the evening,</i>

17:07.090 --> 17:17.840
<i>and the love we shared 
as the stars fell around us.</i>

17:12.870 --> 17:17.840
Um, excuse us. We have some questions.

17:19.080 --> 17:23.530
<i>I'll turn them into a song...</i>

17:25.480 --> 17:27.680
Excuse us!

17:25.730 --> 17:27.690
<b>Excuse us!</b>

17:33.080 --> 17:35.700
Ow...

17:39.300 --> 17:41.200
Y-You...

17:41.200 --> 17:43.680
Wait! Who are you?

17:43.680 --> 17:47.000
What? There should be 
no one left in this city.

17:47.000 --> 17:50.210
Don't scare me like that, damn it.

17:51.080 --> 17:55.220
U-Um, we're merely travelers passing through.

17:56.430 --> 17:59.080
I thought my heart was going to stop.

17:59.690 --> 18:01.230
Sorry.

18:03.360 --> 18:05.750
Hup.

18:06.720 --> 18:09.130
Why did you come here?

18:09.130 --> 18:12.070
As you can see, there's nothing here.

18:12.070 --> 18:14.220
Are you touring abandoned ruins?

18:14.220 --> 18:16.590
We could ask you the same thing.

18:16.590 --> 18:18.980
Why are you the only one left here?

18:23.650 --> 18:25.850
Because I'm a prisoner?

18:39.740 --> 18:43.050
Huh? We're leaving already, Adonis?

18:43.510 --> 18:47.080
We have no business here. Besides...

18:48.110 --> 18:49.760
This place disgusts me.

18:49.760 --> 18:51.090
What?

18:52.200 --> 18:55.770
No business here, huh?

18:58.280 --> 19:03.520
That's what they all said 
when they left this city.

19:05.540 --> 19:07.920
The Gear Expansion...

19:08.760 --> 19:13.520
They said humans couldn't 
live such old-fashioned lives

19:13.530 --> 19:17.550
now that witches had been wiped out.

19:18.040 --> 19:22.550
The future of humanity... Hope and pride...

19:22.550 --> 19:30.250
They packed up all their grand fantasies 
and moved away from this place.

19:31.160 --> 19:36.440
Doesn't it remind you 
of the start of the witch hunts?

19:37.640 --> 19:43.340
In this age, we all follow 
whoever raises their voice first.

19:45.370 --> 19:48.440
Is there a metropolis nearby?

19:49.180 --> 19:54.710
The city-state of Mamuta is 
about 70 kilometers east of here.

19:54.710 --> 19:57.720
I see. Let's go, Doroka.

19:57.720 --> 19:59.080
Okay.

20:00.280 --> 20:04.340
Sorry to have interrupted your song.

20:04.780 --> 20:06.800
Wait for me, Adonis.

20:12.360 --> 20:13.850
Adonis!

20:14.380 --> 20:16.960
Hey, wait up!

20:20.150 --> 20:23.730
That man is going to starve to death.

20:24.150 --> 20:26.400
There's nobody left in the city.

20:26.400 --> 20:30.150
I know he's a prisoner, 
but maybe we could free him.

20:30.150 --> 20:32.000
It's none of our business.

20:33.220 --> 20:39.470
Th-Then, how about we give him 
some of the food Mr. Punch gave us?

20:41.820 --> 20:43.400
Listen...

20:43.960 --> 20:46.650
Was that cell locked?

20:46.650 --> 20:47.640
What?

20:54.350 --> 20:58.200
What that married couple needs isn't food.

20:58.710 --> 20:59.990
Married couple?

21:00.880 --> 21:04.840
What they need is peace and quiet.

21:09.370 --> 21:13.180
I should keep singing my song, Sasha...

21:22.280 --> 21:27.630
It's all right. They're all gone now.

21:36.180 --> 21:48.240
All the people who accused you of being 
a witch and locked you in here are gone now.

21:49.240 --> 21:50.650
From now on,

21:58.160 --> 22:00.950
we'll be together.

22:05.000 --> 22:13.160
I'm sorry I couldn't 
protect you then, Sasha.

22:22.680 --> 22:27.690
This city only needs enough 
room for those two now.

22:29.860 --> 22:31.320
Now let's go...

22:33.480 --> 22:34.830
to Mamuta.
